      "content": "the issue isn't just aging or transcription errors, i know my own body. the primary conflict is in the bone density markers and original ocular pigment documentation from the 1874 correspondence. the society is using those specific metrics to verify my lineage/disposition. if the data says one thing and i am clearly the source of those original texts, how do i frame this divergence as a biological anomaly rather than a failure of proof? i need a way to explain this that won't make them doubt the authenticity of my presence here.",
